# The pages that have a size budget, and what it is.
#
# One line per page: the path, the most lines it may run to, and -- for a page
# that is meant to be an outline -- the most lines any one section may hold,
# where a section is an H2 heading and everything under it to the next one,
# its subsections included. `scripts/check-docs.sh --budget` reads this and
# the Documentation job runs it, so a section pasted back in is red on the day
# it is pasted. Each number carries a sentence on why it is that number and
# not a larger one; raising one is a decision about who the page is for.

# The guide is a path from a clean machine to a running application, and then
# an outline of where everything else is. 300 lines is what that path takes
# when every other topic is a link; the guide was 1,981 lines when only the
# first 520 were the path, and the rest was where a newcomer stopped reading.
# 40 lines a section is what keeps each step something a reader can see whole
# on one screen -- a section that needs more is a topic, and a topic has its
# own page.
DEVELOPERS.md 300 40

# The contract a contributor signs: the Definition of Done, the documentation
# rules, and how a change reaches main. A long CONTRIBUTING turns away exactly
# the people it is for, so 150 is a ceiling rather than a target: a page at
# it has no room for the next sentence, and the answer when one is needed is
# to shorten something or link out, never to raise this.
CONTRIBUTING.md 150
